                <head>267. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On August 3, Secretary McNamara called
                    Secretary Rusk at 11:05 a.m. to say that
                    the President thought it would be wise for them to brief Congressional leaders
                    concerning the Maddox incident. McNamara
                    had already made arrangements for the Secretaries to brief the Senate Armed
                    Services and Foreign Relations Committees at 3 p.m. and the Speaker of the House
                    and selected Congressmen at 4. (Department of State, Rusk Files: Lot 72 D 192,
                    Telephone Conversations) No records of the briefings have been found.</p>
            </div>
